<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal's TAP Q1 operating loss falls.</title>
<headline>Portugal's TAP Q1 operating loss falls.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan 1 to Mar 31:</p>
<p>(billion escudos, unless stated)</p>
<p>Operating result 1.497 loss vs 4.085 loss</p>
<p>Turnover 39.0 vs 37.4  </p>
<p>NOTE: Portuguese state airline TAP-Air Portugal said the number of passengers transported by the airline rose 13.2 percent in the first quarter, compared with the first quarter of 1996. It said that its first quarter results paved the way for a good performance for the remainder of the year. TAP said it forecast a cash flow of 11.4 billion escudos in 1997, compared with a negative cash flow of 0.807 billion in 1996. At the end of March this year, TAP employed 7,405 workers, that is 891 less than the same year-ago period.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +(351-1) 3538254</p>
